WEBVTT

NOTE English translation of the Igbo interview (BBC News Igbo). Working translation; review by a native speaker pending.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Ebonyi is the poorest state in Nigeria today.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Look at the people hawking on the streets: 80 or 90 percent of them are from Ebonyi State.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:19.000
As Governor, within three months, if you see anyone hawking on the street,

4
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.000
know that the person is not from Ebonyi, because I will bring out a plan

5
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.000
that stops them from hawking on the streets.

6
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.000
I am running to be Governor of Ebonyi State.

7
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.000
When I ran in 2023, the people of Ebonyi supported me,

8
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.000
they supported me well.

9
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.000
But many things happened because of the kind of country we live in.

10
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
That is why I pursued it all the way to the Supreme Court of Nigeria.

11
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.000
A lot came out of it.

12
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.000
I decided to hand it over to God, because I know everything is in God's hands.

13
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.000
But one thing I said when I declared that I wanted to run for Governor:

14
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.000
if even 40 percent of what is happening in Abia State were happening in Ebonyi,

15
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
I would not be running for Governor; I would encourage it to continue. But because

16
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.000
I don't see even 10 percent, that is why I am running.

17
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.000
My wife is a woman, and I have a daughter.

18
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.000
My mother is a woman.

19
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Today, my mother is a widow.

20
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:24.000
I know the pain a woman goes through when her husband dies.

21
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.000
The pain they go through raising their children.

22
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Another thing: the woman is the pillar of the home.

23
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.000
So to support a woman is to support the family.

24
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.000
Support a woman, and you have supported the whole community.

25
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:45.000
If God gives me victory, and men make up 60 percent of the government,

26
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.000
women will be 40 percent of those who work with me,

27
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.000
by God's grace, because I know what they are capable of.

28
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.000
I am running on the PDP platform.

29
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.000
I have not left the PDP.

30
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.000
Nothing will make the PDP die.

31
00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.000
If the party were dead, my name would not be on INEC's register.

32
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:03.000
What matters now is the candidate.

33
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.000
That is what will decide Nigerian elections from now on.

34
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:13.000
Politicians must learn that they need good character,

35
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:17.000
because party politics in Nigeria will change one day.

36
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:25.000
The first reason I am going into government is to show what government can do.

37
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:29.000
The second is to bring out policies that will promote business.

38
00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.000
I know how to do it.

39
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.000
Remember that for the past 21 years I have been in a ministry of service,

40
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.000
supporting people.

41
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:40.000
With my own hands I have built roads in the past.

42
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.000
I have provided electricity, built houses for 158 people,

43
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.000
given people free education,

44
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.000
and run medical outreach every year.

45
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.000
So what is governance?

46
00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.000
Governance is for the welfare of the people.

47
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:05.000
If I can do these things through the plans I use to run my foundation,

48
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.000
then I will make it multiply.

49
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:12.000
Come to Ebonyi: the reason there are attacks in our communities is poverty.

50
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.000
If farmers can farm their land, there will be no trouble.

51
00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:23.000
If young people are supported, none of them will go into the bush

52
00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.000
looking for someone to kill.

53
00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.000
It is poverty.

54
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:33.000
That is why government must stand firm on changing the mindset of Ebonyi people

55
00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.000
and rescuing them from poverty.

56
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:39.000
Ebonyi is a land blessed by God, but the problem we have in Ebonyi State

57
00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:44.000
today is leadership.

58
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.000
Get a good leader who understands governance,

59
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.000
and everything will change in the blink of an eye.

60
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:55.000
Many people think you must be in office for eight or twenty years

61
00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:59.000
before you produce visible results.

62
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:04.000
But if you have a plan, if you know the process,

63
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:09.000
change will begin on your first day in office.

64
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.000
A governance plan tells people what your government intends,

65
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.000
and makes people begin to trust government.

66
00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:20.000
When they trust the government, the government can begin to work for the public.

